--
-- Test Description
-- This test is based on tx_und_err_fifo from fifo configuration
-- but has been modified for 64b dma bus width.
-- This test checks the operation of the TX exposed FIFO interface (read).
-- 
-- Functional Coverage
-- * Checks the operation of the tx_r_underflow signal
-- * Checks the operation of the tx_r_err signal
-- 
-- Detailed Test Description
--  1. Initialise suitable FIFO latencies and delays for the test.
--  2. Enable fifo interface using apb write.
--     Check reset values of registers and setup interrupts and then enable 
--     transmit in 100M half duplex mode from a 128-bit FIFO data bus.
--
--  tx_r_underflow testing
--  ----------------------
--  3. Transmit a 64 byte frame. On the first FIFO read operation, signal an
--     underflow by driving the tx_r_underflow signal.
--     Ensure that the TX MAC terminates ongoing transmission correctly,
--     and that an underflow interrupt and status is reported.
--  4. Transmit a 64 byte frame. On the second FIFO read operation, signal an
--     underflow by driving the tx_r_underflow signal.
--     Ensure that the TX MAC terminates ongoing transmission correctly,
--     and that an underflow interrupt and status is reported.
--  5. Transmit a 64 byte frame. On the last FIFO read operation, signal an
--     underflow by driving the tx_r_underflow signal.
--     Ensure that the TX MAC terminates ongoing transmission correctly,
--     and that an underflow interrupt and status is reported.
--  6. Transmit a 16 byte frame. On the first (and last) FIFO read operation,
--     signal an underflow by driving the tx_r_underflow signal.
--     Ensure that the TX MAC terminates ongoing transmission correctly,
--     and that an underflow interrupt and status is reported.
--  7. Transmit a 64 byte frame. Keep tx_r_data_rdy high after the EOP read,
--     so that the TX MAC pre-reads the next frame. On the first FIFO read 
--     operation for the 2nd frame signal an underflow by driving the 
--     tx_r_underflow signal.
--     Ensure that the TX MAC completes the first frame correctly and then
--     terminates the second frame transmission correctly. Also check that
--     an underflow interrupt and status is reported.
--  8. Transmit a 64 byte frame. Keep tx_r_data_rdy high after the EOP read,
--     so that the TX MAC pre-reads the next frame. On the first FIFO (& last)
--     read operation for the 2nd frame signal an underflow by driving the 
--     tx_r_underflow signal.
--     Ensure that the TX MAC completes the first frame correctly and then
--     terminates the second frame transmission correctly. Also check that
--     an underflow interrupt and status is reported.
--  9. Check statistics for above operations.
--
--  tx_r_err testing
--  ----------------
--  Note that no interrupts are generated by tx_r_err when using exposed
--  FIFO interface.
-- 10. Transmit a 64 byte frame. On the first FIFO read operation, signal an
--     error by driving the tx_r_err signal.
--     Ensure that the TX MAC effectively ignores the frame. No transmission
--     will be started and no status or interrupts generated.
-- 11. Transmit a 64 byte frame. On the second FIFO read operation, signal an
--     error by driving the tx_r_err signal.
--     Ensure that the TX MAC terminates ongoing transmission correctly,
--     but that no interupts or status is reported.
-- 12. Transmit a 64 byte frame. On the last FIFO read operation, signal an
--     error by driving the tx_r_err signal.
--     Ensure that the TX MAC terminates ongoing transmission correctly,
--     but that no interupts or status is reported.
-- 13. Transmit a 16 byte frame. On the first (and last) FIFO read operation,
--     signal an error by driving the tx_r_err signal.
--     Ensure that the TX MAC effectively ignores the frame. No transmission
--     will be started and no status or interrupts generated.
-- 14. Transmit a 64 byte frame. Keep tx_r_data_rdy high after the EOP read,
--     so that the TX MAC pre-reads the next frame. On the first FIFO read 
--     operation for the 2nd frame signal an error by driving the 
--     tx_r_err signal.
--     Ensure that the TX MAC completes the first frame correctly and then
--     effectively ignores the 2nd frame frame. No transmission for the 2nd 
--     frame will be started and no status or interrupts generated.
-- 15. Transmit a 64 byte frame. Keep tx_r_data_rdy high after the EOP read,
--     so that the TX MAC pre-reads the next frame. On the first FIFO (& last)
--     read operation for the 2nd frame signal an error by driving the 
--     tx_r_err signal.
--     Ensure that the TX MAC completes the first frame correctly and then
--     effectively ignores the 2nd frame frame. No transmission for the 2nd 
--     frame will be started and no status or interrupts generated.
-- 16. Check statistics for above operations.
--
--  Combined tx_r_underflow & tx_r_err testing
--  ------------------------------------------
-- 17. Transmit a 64 byte frame. On the first FIFO read operation, signal an
--     underflow and an error by driving both tx_r_err & tx_r_underflow.
--     Ensure that the TX MAC terminates ongoing transmission correctly,
--     and that an underflow interrupt and status is reported.
-- 18. Transmit a 64 byte frame. On the second FIFO read operation, signal an
--     underflow and an error by driving both tx_r_err & tx_r_underflow.
--     Ensure that the TX MAC terminates ongoing transmission correctly,
--     and that an underflow interrupt and status is reported.
-- 19. Transmit a 64 byte frame. On the last FIFO read operation, signal an
--     underflow and an error by driving both tx_r_err & tx_r_underflow.
--     Ensure that the TX MAC terminates ongoing transmission correctly,
--     and that an underflow interrupt and status is reported.
-- 20. Transmit a 16 byte frame. On the first (and last) FIFO read operation,
--     signal an underflow and an error by driving both tx_r_err & 
--     tx_r_underflow.
--     Ensure that the TX MAC terminates ongoing transmission correctly,
--     and that an underflow interrupt and status is reported.
-- 21. Check statistics for above operations.
--
--  Status update underflow
--  ------------------------------------------
-- 22. Transmit a 64 byte frame. Keep tx_r_data_rdy high after the EOP read,
--     so that the TX MAC pre-reads the next frame. Then supply a one-byte
--     frame with no CRC/padding specified.
--     Because of the delay in tb_fifo status handshaking, the second frame
--     should complete before the handshaking has completed for the first frame.
--     Ensure that the TX MAC completes the first frame correctly and then
--     successfully transmits the second frame, but signals an underrun status
--     and interrupt for the second frame.
-- 23. Check statistics for above operations.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------


--******************************************************************************
--  1. Initialise suitable FIFO latencies and delays for the test.
--******************************************************************************
fifo_latency      3
fifo_under_delay  3
fifo_status_delay 5



--******************************************************************************
--  2. Check reset values of registers and setup interrupts and then enable 
--     transmit in 100M half duplex mode from a 128-bit FIFO data bus.
--******************************************************************************
apbwr(60)  4c 00000001  -- enable soft config fifo port bit when available
apbrd      4c 00000001  -- check enable soft config bit when available

apbrd(100) 00 00000000  -- check reset value of network control register
apbrd      04 00080000  -- check reset value of network config register
apbrd      08 00000006  -- check reset value of network status register
apbwr      28 ffffffff  -- enable all interrupts
apbrd      24 00000000  -- check interrupt status
apbrd      30 00000000  -- check that all interrupts are now enabled
apbwr      04 00680000  -- enable 100M mode into 128-bit bus
apbwr      00 00000008  -- enable transmit
apbrd      14 00000000  -- check tx status, wait for tx_go when enabled
apbrd      14 00000008  -- check tx status, always tx_go when enabled



--******************************************************************************
--  3. Transmit a 64 byte frame. On the first FIFO read operation, signal an
--     underflow by driving the tx_r_underflow signal.
--     Ensure that the TX MAC terminates ongoing transmission correctly,
--     and that an underflow interrupt and status is reported.
--******************************************************************************

apbrdf     14 00000008  "Scenario 1: TX FIFO underflow - SOP"
                        -- check tx status, always tx_go in fifo mode
                        -- and trigger data ready for first frame

-- Supply data to TX FIFO interface
--
-- CONTROL =  <RESERVED>, NO CRC, FLUSH, UNDERFLOW, RDY, ERR, SOP, EOP.
--
--              CONTROL   MOD  STATUS          DATA
fifo_rd(apb)    01011010   0   00001000    8877665544332211 -- UNDERFLOW
-- no more FIFO data reads

-- No data presented as SOP not successfully read

-- No status update on SOP underrun



--******************************************************************************
--  4. Transmit a 64 byte frame. On the second FIFO read operation, signal an
